  "body": "Found while gating the merge of main into PR #1157 (quick gate, Linux, debug). Reproduced on a clean worktree of upstream/main at c69e839a, so it is not from that PR.\n\n`cargo test -p camcraft-app --test stepped_stock_rapid` - 7 passed, 1 failed, deterministic:\n\n```\n---- a_coarse_stock_whose_source_is_gone_is_never_acquitted stdout ----\npanicked at crates/app/tests/stepped_stock_rapid.rs:274:23:\nPart: not blocked by the rapid law: post blocked - Op1: model 'casting' was imported too coarsely to verify; re-import with a larger STEP facet budget (surfaces are approximated to within 2.500 mm)\n```\n\nThe post is still blocked (no unsafe output), but by the coarse-import refusal instead of the rapid-in-stock law the test pins (`rapid move {at} `). Either the refusal order changed on main (a coarse-model door now runs ahead of the rapid law), or the test's expectation needs updating to accept that door. Which one is right needs a look at the PR that added the coarse-import refusal.\n\nDone means: the test passes on main, with the intended refusal named, and the reason recorded.\n",
